WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.767 --> 00:00:02.201
[music playing]

00:00:02.268 --> 00:00:02.802
GRADY POWELL: Well, gentlemen,
congratulations to the two

00:00:02.902 --> 00:00:03.902
of you.

00:00:04.003 --> 00:00:05.538
You have beat out
the competition

00:00:05.605 --> 00:00:07.039
in the first and second round
of our Arctic Forge Challenge,

00:00:07.106 --> 00:00:08.340
which means you're
both one step closer

00:00:08.440 --> 00:00:10.643
to check for $10,000
and the title of "Forged

00:00:10.709 --> 00:00:11.978
in Fire" Champion.

00:00:12.045 --> 00:00:13.546
Now, guys, in this final
round of competition,

00:00:13.613 --> 00:00:15.348
we're going to send you
back to your home forges

00:00:15.414 --> 00:00:19.319
to build yet another iconic
weapon from the ice cold North.

00:00:19.385 --> 00:00:23.690
And that weapon is the
Northern Long Seax.

00:00:26.425 --> 00:00:28.328
DAVID BAKER: The Northern Long
Seax is a single-edged blade

00:00:28.395 --> 00:00:31.697
widely used by Vikings and
northern European tribes

00:00:31.764 --> 00:00:33.566
during the Middle Ages.

00:00:33.666 --> 00:00:36.569
Its razor-sharp edge and pointed
tip were useful in slashing

00:00:36.669 --> 00:00:39.639
as well as for thrusting,
allowing the user to deliver

00:00:39.739 --> 00:00:42.508
heavy blows and stabs to
finish off an opponent

00:00:42.608 --> 00:00:44.410
in close quarter combat.

00:00:44.477 --> 00:00:46.012
Although used as
a deadly weapon,

00:00:46.078 --> 00:00:47.947
the Vikings would also
use the Seax to hack

00:00:48.013 --> 00:00:51.050
tree branches and skin animals.

00:00:51.117 --> 00:00:52.585
Today, the versatile
blade can be

00:00:52.652 --> 00:00:55.822
seen in Netflix historical
drama series "The Last Kingdom."

00:00:55.888 --> 00:00:58.524
 Now, guys, you only have four
days to build these blades,

00:00:58.591 --> 00:01:01.027
and when you come back, we
want to see two Seaxes that are

00:01:01.093 --> 00:01:03.029
worth at least $10,000 apiece.

00:01:03.096 --> 00:01:05.331
Because that's what one
of them will win you.

00:01:05.432 --> 00:01:05.998
Good luck, guys.

00:01:06.098 --> 00:01:07.033
We'll see in four days.

00:01:07.133 --> 00:01:07.833
 Good luck.

00:01:07.900 --> 00:01:08.668
 Yeah.

00:01:11.604 --> 00:01:12.938
DEVON CHATTERLEY:
I'm Devon Chatterley.

00:01:13.038 --> 00:01:14.240
I'm 29 years old.

00:01:14.340 --> 00:01:16.643 line:8%
I am an active
National Guardsman,

00:01:16.709 --> 00:01:19.078
and I am a part-time bladesmith.

00:01:19.145 --> 00:01:22.082
I need to come in here
gung ho-- full focus.

00:01:22.182 --> 00:01:24.083
I'm ready to become the next
"Forged in Fire" Champion

00:01:24.149 --> 00:01:26.018
and join the other
winners before me.

00:01:26.085 --> 00:01:27.587
Oh my gosh!

00:01:27.687 --> 00:01:30.356
I noticed that it concaved
going up to the drop point,

00:01:30.423 --> 00:01:32.258
so I'm going to
start drawing out

00:01:32.358 --> 00:01:33.993
that metal wide as possible.

00:01:34.093 --> 00:01:36.062
Because I need this
to make parameters.

00:01:36.162 --> 00:01:37.130
There we go.

00:01:37.230 --> 00:01:38.598
That's the one I
was looking for!

00:01:38.665 --> 00:01:41.868
I couldn't be more proud.

00:01:41.934 --> 00:01:43.202
Let's get started on the handle.

00:01:43.269 --> 00:01:45.238
I'm going to cut
up some aluminum

00:01:45.338 --> 00:01:46.739
bar stock for the pommel.

00:01:46.839 --> 00:01:47.940
It threads.

00:01:48.007 --> 00:01:48.775
Whoo!

00:01:52.145 --> 00:01:53.846
All right.

00:01:53.946 --> 00:01:55.314
Now it's even more snug.

00:01:55.381 --> 00:01:56.916
Today I'm just going to
focus on the little details.

00:01:56.983 --> 00:01:59.018
I know my handle's a
bit plain and bland,

00:01:59.118 --> 00:02:00.453
but at least it'll be shiny.

00:02:00.520 --> 00:02:02.188
I just want to make sure
this weapon will perform,

00:02:02.288 --> 00:02:04.257
so at the end of this
day, I will be testing

00:02:04.357 --> 00:02:06.759
it out as much as I can.

00:02:06.826 --> 00:02:09.429
OK, here we go.

00:02:09.529 --> 00:02:12.798
[laughter]

00:02:12.865 --> 00:02:14.734
Sliced right through.

00:02:14.834 --> 00:02:16.201
I got my blade done!

00:02:16.268 --> 00:02:17.369
I'm very happy with it.

00:02:17.436 --> 00:02:17.903
It cuts.

00:02:17.970 --> 00:02:18.904
It kills.

00:02:18.971 --> 00:02:20.240
It's pretty much perfect.

00:02:24.043 --> 00:02:25.544 line:14%
 My name is Clay Wolf.

00:02:25.644 --> 00:02:27.747 line:8%
I build houses for a living,
and I'm a part time bladesmith.

00:02:27.814 --> 00:02:30.783
I got into smithing by
watching the competition.

00:02:30.850 --> 00:02:34.387
So I bought a forge, and then
I started doing my own at home

00:02:34.454 --> 00:02:36.022
competitions with myself.

00:02:36.088 --> 00:02:38.725
I set a three hour
alarm, and I make

00:02:38.791 --> 00:02:40.426
random parameters for myself.

00:02:40.527 --> 00:02:41.493
And I go at it.

00:02:41.593 --> 00:02:43.529
Those look like they're
setting really well.

00:02:43.596 --> 00:02:44.630
There we go.

00:02:44.730 --> 00:02:47.400
So I decided to put some
detail on my spine--

00:02:47.466 --> 00:02:48.801
make it stand out a little bit.

00:02:48.901 --> 00:02:50.369
I'm just working on my handle.

00:02:50.436 --> 00:02:54.607
And as I'm looking at it, I
notice it has a twist to it.

00:02:54.707 --> 00:02:57.075
I cannot turn
something like that.

00:02:57.176 --> 00:02:59.078
I'm going to stick
it in the forge

00:02:59.144 --> 00:03:01.814
and try to hammer this straight.

00:03:01.881 --> 00:03:05.684
There's a slight warp,
but that'll have to do.

00:03:05.751 --> 00:03:09.221
Well, we got the forge
lit, so we might as well

00:03:09.321 --> 00:03:11.524
try to heat treat this thing.

00:03:16.695 --> 00:03:17.664
Hard.

00:03:17.764 --> 00:03:19.432
Good quench, good quench.

00:03:19.532 --> 00:03:23.069
This wood I'm using is walnut,
and what's special about this

00:03:23.135 --> 00:03:25.270
is this tree grew
on my family farm

00:03:25.337 --> 00:03:28.140
and was cut down on
our family saw mill.

00:03:28.207 --> 00:03:29.875
And it looks amazing.

00:03:29.975 --> 00:03:31.477
I couldn't be happier.

00:03:31.543 --> 00:03:33.846
I have an edge on
this, but I really

00:03:33.913 --> 00:03:35.181
want to see how sharp it is.

00:03:35.247 --> 00:03:36.816
So I need to test this blade.

00:03:36.882 --> 00:03:39.786
I really hope that this is going
to cut through these bottles

00:03:39.886 --> 00:03:41.353
with ease.

00:03:41.453 --> 00:03:45.591
I hope my blade's sharp enough,
but we're going to find out.

00:03:45.691 --> 00:03:48.194
This blade just cut right
through the water bottles

00:03:48.261 --> 00:03:49.028
with ease.

00:03:49.095 --> 00:03:50.229
They're clean cuts.

00:03:50.329 --> 00:03:51.597
I couldn't be happier.

00:03:51.664 --> 00:03:53.933
I feel confident sending
this back to the forge.

00:03:53.999 --> 00:03:55.234
I can't wait to see it tested.

00:03:55.301 --> 00:03:56.469
DOUG MARCAIDA: All
right, bladesmiths.

00:03:56.536 --> 00:03:59.371
Welcome to the KEAL test.

00:03:59.471 --> 00:04:01.908
To find out what kind of lethal
damage your weapons will do,

00:04:02.008 --> 00:04:04.310
I will take your weapon and
deliver some lethal blows

00:04:04.377 --> 00:04:06.245
on this pig carcass.

00:04:06.345 --> 00:04:07.480
Clay, are you ready to play?

00:04:07.547 --> 00:04:08.547
 Yes, sir.

00:04:08.614 --> 00:04:09.582
DOUG MARCAIDA: All
right, let's do this.

00:04:25.097 --> 00:04:26.799
 Whoa!

00:04:26.866 --> 00:04:28.368
[music playing]

00:04:28.434 --> 00:04:31.571
 All right, let's talk about
your Northern Long Seax here.

00:04:31.637 --> 00:04:33.872
You have a forward heavy blade.

00:04:33.972 --> 00:04:39.211
With that forward weight, it
really allows for deeper chops.

00:04:39.278 --> 00:04:40.980
The edges are sharp.

00:04:41.047 --> 00:04:42.515
They cut deep.

00:04:42.581 --> 00:04:45.317
And overall, sir, your weapon--

00:04:45.384 --> 00:04:46.385
it'll KEAL.

00:04:46.451 --> 00:04:48.421
 That's all I wanted to hear.

00:04:48.521 --> 00:04:50.489
 All right, dapper Devon.

00:04:50.589 --> 00:04:51.858
You're up next.
Are you ready, sir?

00:04:51.924 --> 00:04:53.026
 I'm pumped.
Let's do this.

00:05:16.215 --> 00:05:18.117
 Nice.

00:05:18.184 --> 00:05:19.251
 Thanks, man.

00:05:19.318 --> 00:05:20.052
[music playing]

00:05:20.152 --> 00:05:21.219
 All right, Devon.

00:05:21.320 --> 00:05:23.088
Let's talk about
your weapon here.

00:05:23.189 --> 00:05:24.623
The blade you have
here is nicely

00:05:24.690 --> 00:05:27.493
balanced-- that when
I cut, the weapon

00:05:27.593 --> 00:05:29.228
does not do the work for me.

00:05:29.294 --> 00:05:31.397
I do the work with every slash.

00:05:31.464 --> 00:05:35.534
As you can see, I cut it down
twice all the way through.

00:05:35.601 --> 00:05:40.006
Overall, sir, your Northern
Long Seax will KEAL.

00:05:40.073 --> 00:05:40.840
 Thank you, sir.

00:05:45.411 --> 00:05:47.747
J. NEILSON: Bladesmiths,
welcome to our strength test.

00:05:47.813 --> 00:05:49.748
Fittingly for this
Arctic Challenge,

00:05:49.815 --> 00:05:52.985
we're going to do
the ice block chop.

00:05:53.085 --> 00:05:55.388
It really tests the edge
holding and overall construct

00:05:55.454 --> 00:05:58.958
of your knives, and
it's a lot of fun, too.

00:05:59.025 --> 00:05:59.725
Clay, you're first.

00:05:59.792 --> 00:06:00.426
You ready to go?

00:06:00.493 --> 00:06:02.929
 Give her hell.

00:06:03.029 --> 00:06:05.965
[grunting]

00:06:20.947 --> 00:06:22.181
[music playing]

00:06:22.281 --> 00:06:24.483
 All right, Clay, I've got a
little bit of an issue here.

00:06:24.550 --> 00:06:27.352
Your grain's not that bad.

00:06:27.453 --> 00:06:29.989
I mean, it could be finer,
but it's not that bad.

00:06:30.055 --> 00:06:34.861
But every time I hit, that
blade vibrated like crazy.

00:06:34.961 --> 00:06:36.262
And it just traveled down.

00:06:36.329 --> 00:06:38.264
So it started to
bend, and then all

00:06:38.330 --> 00:06:41.500
that vibration and everything--
it just finally came loose.

00:06:41.567 --> 00:06:42.935
I hate to see a nice
Damascus pattern

00:06:43.002 --> 00:06:45.037
like this have something
happen to it like that,

00:06:45.138 --> 00:06:48.007
but, hey, it was
a good fight, man.

00:06:52.811 --> 00:06:54.414
GRADY POWELL: We
hate to see it, Clay.

00:06:54.480 --> 00:06:56.616
Unfortunately, your blade
did succumb to this test.

00:06:56.682 --> 00:06:58.484
But you're not out
of the fight yet.

00:06:58.550 --> 00:07:02.388
Devon, you have to survive
six blows in the same test

00:07:02.488 --> 00:07:04.923
to claim the title and
the check for $10,000.

00:07:04.990 --> 00:07:05.491
You ready?

00:07:05.558 --> 00:07:06.526
 Let's do it.

00:07:15.501 --> 00:07:18.671
[grunting]

00:07:36.455 --> 00:07:38.123
 Devon, congratulations, man.

00:07:38.190 --> 00:07:39.258
 Thank you.

00:07:39.358 --> 00:07:40.792
GRADY POWELL: Clay--
difficult test.

00:07:40.859 --> 00:07:42.694
And I want to say, thank you
so much for your hard work.

00:07:42.794 --> 00:07:45.363
But unfortunately, due to
the catastrophic failure,

00:07:45.464 --> 00:07:46.933
we couldn't continue
the testing.

00:07:46.999 --> 00:07:49.635
So unfortunately, man, your time
here in the forge has ended,

00:07:49.701 --> 00:07:51.403
and I have to ask you
to please step out.

00:07:51.470 --> 00:07:52.605
 Thank you.

00:07:52.671 --> 00:07:54.473
 Well, Devon,
congratulations, man.

00:07:54.539 --> 00:07:58.344
You are today's
Arctic Forge Champion.

00:07:58.444 --> 00:07:59.712
You absolutely deserve it.

00:07:59.778 --> 00:08:01.313
That is a brutal test,
and you crushed it.

00:08:01.413 --> 00:08:02.114
[clapping]

00:08:02.181 --> 00:08:03.249
 Thank you.

00:08:03.349 --> 00:08:05.383
I can't believe
this just happened.

00:08:05.484 --> 00:08:07.119
I am the "Forged
in Fire" Champion!

00:08:07.219 --> 00:08:10.689
And I'm just thanking all the
support I've had from my wife.

00:08:10.789 --> 00:08:12.691
My first plan is to
take my wife to Miami.

00:08:12.791 --> 00:08:14.327
We're going to get out
of this cold weather

00:08:14.427 --> 00:08:16.128
and go sit on the beach
for at least four days

00:08:16.228 --> 00:08:17.830
and just relax in the sunlight.

00:08:17.930 --> 00:08:19.966
I'm very excited.

